WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.185
Lesson 2.3.

00:00:02.185 --> 00:00:03.750
Providing liquidity.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:05.837
By the end, you'll be able to

00:00:05.837 --> 00:00:08.758
estimate an LP position's fee income from

00:00:08.758 --> 00:00:11.540
real pool data, before you ever deposit.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.130
Here's the plan.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:17.408
First, what you actually receive when you provide liquidity,

00:00:17.408 --> 00:00:20.395
and what changes underneath you while you hold it.

00:00:20.395 --> 00:00:22.651
Second, the fee A.P.R. formula,

00:00:22.651 --> 00:00:24.855
with a real worked example.

00:00:24.855 --> 00:00:26.672
And third, the checklist to run

00:00:26.672 --> 00:00:28.545
before you deposit into any pool.

00:00:29.845 --> 00:00:32.905
Providing liquidity is not a savings account.

00:00:32.905 --> 00:00:35.250
You're not just earning a fee for sitting still.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:37.731
You're the counterparty to every single trade

00:00:37.731 --> 00:00:39.835
that happens in that pool, whether the

00:00:39.835 --> 00:00:41.615
price moves in your favor or not.

00:00:42.915 --> 00:00:44.100
What you actually get.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.530
When you L.P., you deposit both tokens, and

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:51.234
you receive a share of the pool back,

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:54.577
a fungible token for a full-range position, or

00:00:54.577 --> 00:00:57.225
an N.F.T. for a concentrated one.

00:00:57.225 --> 00:00:58.637
You earn your share of every

00:00:58.637 --> 00:01:00.300
swap fee that pool collects.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.520
In return, your token mix changes as

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.860
traders move the price: you become the

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.620
counterparty to every trade that goes through.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.355
Here's that exchange, start to finish.

00:01:11.355 --> 00:01:13.830
You deposit both tokens into the pool.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.132
The pool issues you a

00:01:15.132 --> 00:01:17.800
position, representing your exact share.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.786
From that point on, you earn a slice

00:01:19.786 --> 00:01:22.125
of every swap fee that passes through.

00:01:22.125 --> 00:01:24.448
And as traders push the price around,

00:01:24.448 --> 00:01:27.015
your own token mix shifts underneath you,

00:01:27.015 --> 00:01:29.765
automatically, to match the pool's new ratio.

00:01:31.065 --> 00:01:32.155
Quick check.

00:01:32.155 --> 00:01:33.963
What do you actually receive when

00:01:33.963 --> 00:01:35.240
you deposit into a pool?

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.984
The answer: a share of the pool,

00:01:41.984 --> 00:01:45.082
a fungible token for a full-range position,

00:01:45.082 --> 00:01:48.250
or an N.F.T. representing a concentrated one.

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:51.525
The fee APR formula.

00:01:52.825 --> 00:01:54.260
Here's the formula.

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:57.961
Fee A.P.R. is approximately daily volume, times the

00:01:57.961 --> 00:02:01.163
fee tier, times your pool share, times three

00:02:01.163 --> 00:02:04.025
sixty five, divided by your deposit.

00:02:04.025 --> 00:02:06.847
For a full-range pool, your share is just your

00:02:06.847 --> 00:02:10.090
deposit divided by the pool's total value locked.

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:14.026
That simplifies the formula to daily volume, times fee

00:02:14.026 --> 00:02:17.747
tier, times three sixty five, divided by T.V.L. And

00:02:17.747 --> 00:02:21.410
use a thirty day average volume, never today's.

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:24.251
A single volatile day overstates your income,

00:02:24.251 --> 00:02:26.598
and that same volatile day is exactly

00:02:26.598 --> 00:02:29.069
when you take the most impermanent loss.

00:02:30.369 --> 00:02:32.414
Work it through on a real pool.

00:02:32.414 --> 00:02:34.794
T.V.L. ten million dollars.

00:02:34.794 --> 00:02:38.229
Thirty day average daily volume, two million dollars.

00:02:38.229 --> 00:02:40.764
Fee tier, zero point three percent.

00:02:40.764 --> 00:02:43.537
Daily pool fees: two million times zero

00:02:43.537 --> 00:02:46.888
point zero zero three, six thousand dollars.

00:02:46.888 --> 00:02:50.121
Your ten thousand dollar deposit is zero point

00:02:50.121 --> 00:02:52.942
one percent of that T.V.L. Your share of

00:02:52.942 --> 00:02:55.443
today's fees: six dollars a day.

00:02:55.443 --> 00:02:58.975
Annualized, that's about twenty one point nine percent

00:02:58.975 --> 00:03:01.800
fee A.P.R., before impermanent loss and gas.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.155
Now watch what moves that number.

00:03:05.155 --> 00:03:08.911
Same pool, volume halves to $1M a day:

00:03:08.911 --> 00:03:13.160
your fee APR halves too, to about 10.95%.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:16.563
Or TVL doubles to $20M, with volume

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:20.722
unchanged: your share shrinks, and your fee

00:03:20.722 --> 00:03:24.520
APR lands at exactly the same 10.95%.

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:26.238
Either one, on its own, cuts

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:27.660
your fee income in half.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:30.050
Quick check.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:33.166
A pool holds five million dollars T.V.L.,

00:03:33.166 --> 00:03:35.466
one million a day in volume, a

00:03:35.466 --> 00:03:38.585
zero point zero five percent fee tier.

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:40.730
What's the full-range fee A.P.R.?

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:48.963
The answer: one million, times zero point zero zero

00:03:48.963 --> 00:03:52.703
zero five, times three sixty five, divided by five

00:03:52.703 --> 00:03:55.710
million, is three point six five percent.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:58.735
Last check for this section.

00:03:58.735 --> 00:04:00.032
Why use a thirty day

00:04:00.032 --> 00:04:02.133
average volume instead of today's?

00:04:06.553 --> 00:04:09.699
The answer: a single volatile day overstates your

00:04:09.699 --> 00:04:12.342
fee income, and that same volatile day is

00:04:12.342 --> 00:04:15.363
exactly when you take the most impermanent loss.

00:04:16.663 --> 00:04:19.008
Where LPs actually lose money.

00:04:20.308 --> 00:04:22.029
Here's how people lose on this

00:04:22.029 --> 00:04:24.049
even after doing the math once.

00:04:24.049 --> 00:04:28.252
Chasing the single highest-A.P.R. pool listed anywhere, without

00:04:28.252 --> 00:04:31.667
checking whether that yield comes from real trading

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:35.053
volume or from a temporary incentive that ends.

00:04:35.053 --> 00:04:38.293
Assuming fees always cover impermanent loss, they

00:04:38.293 --> 00:04:41.703
often don't, especially in a fast-moving market.

00:04:41.703 --> 00:04:45.083
Never recording entry prices, so there's no honest

00:04:45.083 --> 00:04:48.233
vs-hold comparison to catch a bad position.

00:04:48.233 --> 00:04:51.284
And panic-withdrawing after one rough day instead of

00:04:51.284 --> 00:04:53.759
following the exit rule written in advance.

00:04:55.059 --> 00:04:56.254
Before you deposit.

00:04:57.554 --> 00:05:00.214
Run this before you deposit into any pool.

00:05:00.214 --> 00:05:04.610
Calculate fee A.P.R. from thirty day volume, not today's.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:08.133
Confirm you'd genuinely be okay holding one hundred percent

00:05:08.133 --> 00:05:11.545
of either token, since that's the real downside case.

00:05:11.545 --> 00:05:13.590
Record your entry prices, so you

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:16.120
have a real vs-hold benchmark later.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:19.043
And write your exit rule now: volume drops, a

00:05:19.043 --> 00:05:22.410
trend starts, or fees stop covering impermanent loss.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.925
Your turn, 5 to 10 minutes.

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:27.300
Pick a real pool.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:31.036
Pull its TVL and 30-day average volume, and work

00:05:31.036 --> 00:05:34.239
out your fee APR for a deposit size you'd

00:05:34.239 --> 00:05:37.670
actually make, before you ever click confirm.

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:42.324
To recap: providing liquidity means depositing both

00:05:42.324 --> 00:05:45.291
tokens and becoming the counterparty to every

00:05:45.291 --> 00:05:47.720
trade, not just collecting a fee.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:52.184
Fee APR is daily volume, times fee tier, times

00:05:52.184 --> 00:05:57.232
365, divided by TVL, always from a 30-day average.

00:05:57.232 --> 00:06:00.104
And either volume halving or TVL doubling

00:06:00.104 --> 00:06:02.087
cuts your fee income in half.

00:06:03.387 --> 00:06:05.182
That's providing liquidity.

00:06:05.182 --> 00:06:08.961
Next up, Lesson 2.4: impermanent loss, and your LP

00:06:08.961 --> 00:06:13.037
position's true profit and loss against simply holding.
